# tally 2.3.1 R1, #248 face (b) (L §8: on an operand that is a hole the check isn't made; E §4.2 step 5): a
# lifespan's end with a hole balance is the balance's hole (s_end, the `?` amount); a known balance is still
# refused (s_p60) or 0 (s_p100). Before: s_end RUN-LIFESPAN holding the known part.
=== life_amt.tally
model life
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place spare: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..2026-06-30
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input out_amt: money PLN
input out_day: date

move empty: transfers
  on out_day
  leg cash from spare to konto amount out_amt

ask s_may: bal(spare, 2026-05-31)
ask s_end: bal(spare, 2026-06-30)
ask k_end: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)
ask k_jul: bal(konto, 2026-07-31)
ask s_p100: bal(spare, 2026-06-30) with out_amt = 100.00 PLN
ask s_p60: bal(spare, 2026-06-30) with out_amt = 60.00 PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[spare] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  out_amt = ?"how much was moved out?" "s"
  out_day = 2026-03-10 "s"
=== expect
k_end: ?"how much was moved out?" (out_amt)
  unfulfilled: empty
  cut 2026-06-30
k_jul: ?"how much was moved out?" (out_amt)
  unfulfilled: empty
  cut 2026-06-30
s_end: ?"how much was moved out?" (out_amt)
  unfulfilled: empty
  cut 2026-06-30
s_may: ?"how much was moved out?" (out_amt)
  unfulfilled: empty
  cut 2026-06-30
s_p100: 0.00 PLN
  pinned: out_amt = 100.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: empty
  cut 2026-06-30
s_p60: refused: RUN-LIFESPAN spare ends on 2026-06-30 holding 40.00 PLN
  pinned: out_amt = 60.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: empty
  cut 2026-06-30
